---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const cases = [
  {
    title: 'A payments system that <strong>pays people on time</strong>',
    body: [
      'For a ticketing and e-commerce platform I built and run, I designed the money path end to end: card and wallet checkout across two processors, fees and taxes computed per line, refunds and partial refunds, and automated payouts to hundreds of organizers in two countries and currencies. Every dollar is traceable from the order to the settlement it landed in, which is what makes disputes and accounting boring instead of dramatic.',
      'The interesting work was in the edges: early payouts before an event with a true-up afterwards, foreign-currency settlement that fails closed rather than guessing, and reconciliation that catches drift between the processor and the ledger before a customer does.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'An event-management system <strong>operators actually use</strong>',
    body: [
      'The same platform runs live events from announcement to door: showtimes, tiered and time-limited pricing, seated venues with interactive seat maps, passes, waitlists, resale, and check-in on a phone at the door. Operators manage it from an admin that was built with them watching, so the workflows match how a venue really runs a night rather than how a database is shaped.',
      "It's an Elixir/Phoenix system with multi-region data residency, event-sourced inventory so a seat can't be sold twice, and a small senior team shipping to it daily. Thousands of events have gone through it.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Ads management <strong>inside the product</strong>',
    body: [
      "Organizers were spending real money on social ads and couldn't connect it to ticket sales. I built an ads layer into the platform: campaigns created and published from the event page, pixel and server-side conversion tracking wired to actual purchases, and reporting that shows what an ad made, not just what it cost.",
      'The hard part was the integration surface: a third-party ads API that changes under you, half-published states to recover from, and attribution that stays honest when a customer sees an ad on one device and buys on another.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Scaling an engineering org from 20 to 150 <strong>without breaking it</strong>',
    body: [
      'At a global engineering services firm, the engineering organization had to grow roughly sevenfold without losing delivery quality. I built a management layer rather than a flat team, hired and developed the managers and technical leads under it, and kept practices like TDD and pairing in place as headcount climbed. The result was a much larger organization that still delivered, with leadership that could run without me in the room.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Work" description="Selected work: a payments system, an event-management system, ads management built into the product, and scaling an engineering org.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Selected <strong>work</strong></h1>
    <p>A few things I've built or led, told the way I'd tell them over coffee.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="cases">
    {cases.map((c) => (
      <article class="case">
        <h2 set:html={c.title} />
        {c.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:4rem"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk about your situation</a></p>
</Base>
